    "content": "CYTOGENETICS LABORATORY\nFLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) REPORT\n\nPatient Name: [redacted name]\nMedical Record #: [redacted ID]\nDate of Birth: [redacted date]\nSpecimen Type: Bone marrow core biopsy\nDate Collected: [redacted date]\nDate Received: [redacted date]\nDate Reported: [redacted date]\n\nCLINICAL INDICATION:\nSuspected MALT-type lymphoma or Hairy cell leukemia\n\nTEST PERFORMED:\nFluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH) on bone marrow core biopsy tissue sections\n\nFISH PANEL:\n1. t(11;18)(q21;q21) API2/MALT1 fusion probe\n2. t(14;18)(q32;q21) IGH/MALT1 fusion probe\n3. t(1;14)(p22;q32) BCL10/IGH fusion probe\n4. t(3;14)(p14.1;q32) FOXP1/IGH fusion probe\n5. Trisomy 3 probe (CEP3)\n6. 7q31 deletion probe\n\nRESULTS:\n\nt(11;18) API2/MALT1:\nResult: NEGATIVE\nNuclei analyzed: 200\nNormal signal pattern: 196/200 (98%)\nCutoff: <5%\n\nt(14;18) IGH/MALT1:\nResult: NEGATIVE\nNuclei analyzed: 200\nNormal signal pattern: 195/200 (97.5%)\nCutoff: <5%\n\nt(1;14) BCL10/IGH:\nResult: NEGATIVE\nNuclei analyzed: 200\nNormal signal pattern: 197/200 (98.5%)\nCutoff: <5%\n\nt(3;14) FOXP1/IGH:\nResult: NEGATIVE\nNuclei analyzed: 200\nNormal signal pattern: 198/200 (99%)\nCutoff: <5%\n\nTrisomy 3:\nResult: NEGATIVE\nNuclei analyzed: 200\nNormal signal pattern (2 signals): 194/200 (97%)\nCutoff: <10%\n\n7q31 deletion:\nResult: NEGATIVE\nNuclei analyzed: 200\nNormal signal pattern (2 signals): 196/200 (98%)\nCutoff: <10%\n\nINTERPRETATION:\nFISH analysis performed on bone marrow core biopsy tissue sections shows no evidence of the common chromosomal abnormalities associated with MALT lymphoma, including t(11;18), t(14;18), t(1;14), t(3;14), or trisomy 3. Additionally, no deletion of 7q31 was detected, which is sometimes seen in hairy cell leukemia.\n\nThese negative results do not exclude the diagnosis of MALT lymphoma or hairy cell leukemia, as not all cases harbor detectable chromosomal abnormalities by FISH. Correlation with morphology, immunophenotype, and clinical findings is recommended.\n\nMETHODOLOGY:\nFISH was performed on 4-micron formalin-fixed, paraffin-embedded tissue sections using commercially available probes according to manufacturer's protocols. A minimum of 200 interphase nuclei were analyzed for each probe set.\n\nReported by: [redacted name], Ph.D.\nLaboratory Director: [redacted name], M.D., Ph.D.",
